{
  "info": {
    "name": "SCRUM-181 Lender collateral analysis: geographic risk context",
    "description": "Manual checks for the geography section of GET /api/lender/applications/{id}/collateral-analysis. See docs/lender-collateral-analysis.md. Run the folders in order with the Collection Runner. Needs a running service (baseUrl), a Keycloak realm (keycloakUrl, clientIdKc) and three users: A and B have the lender realm role, A creates a new organization and its applications, B is not a member; C is signed in without the lender role (folder 5 only). Users must have logged in to GeoZentra once. The property ids are those of the SCRUM-127 checks (docs/location-intelligence-risk.md): idFull every source loaded, idPartial county flood map not loaded, idNoParcel property without parcel; on another database pick them with the SELECTs of that doc. Every run creates a new organization, so the collection can be repeated. Passwords are left empty: set them in your local environment and never commit them.",
